*:\n     - The user questioned why AI server controls were present in \"إعدادات النظام\" (`screen-settings`) when a dedicated \"إدارة السيرفرات\" screen exists.\n  3. **AI Server Terminal Visibility (\"لازم أكبر الشاشة لأكبر حاجة علشان يظهر وكمان بيكون متأكل\")**:\n     - In `screen-servers`, the large active banner and tall cards (~420px each with 2x2 large buttons) pushed `#ai-server-terminal` below the fold, forcing vertical scrolling, window maximization, and clipping.\n  4. **Clicking \"إيقاف السيرفر\" does not stop**:\n     - Standard `taskkill` failed with `Access is denied` because PID 3524 was started as Administrator. `loadServersUI` immediately re-checked port 8000, found it still listening, and reset the button to `إيقاف السيرفر` within milliseconds, appearing unresponsive.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Progress\n### Completed:\n1. **`desktop_app/server_manager.py`**:\n   - Updated `ServerInstance.get_status()` to differentiate between `is_managed` (process launched and tracked by the app) and `is_external` (port listening externally/orphaned).\n   - In `ServerInstance.stop()`: added elevated taskkill fallback via `ctypes.windll.shell32.ShellExecuteW(None, \"runas\", \"cmd.exe\", f\"/c taskkill /F /PID {pid}\", None, 0)`.\n   - Added `MultiServerManager.force_free_ports()` to kill any process holding ports 8000 or 8001.\n2. **`desktop_app/backend.py`**:\n   - Added `API.free_server_ports()` which logs to the AI Server console and calls `force_free_ports()`.\n   - Added `add_server_log()`, `get_server_logs()`, and `clear_server_logs()`.\n3. **`scripts/free_ports.bat`**:\n   - Created batch script in `scripts/free_ports.bat` for 1-click elevation cleanup of ports 8000 and 8001.\n4. **`desktop_app/templates/index.html` (Settings Clean-up)**:\n   - Cleaned `screen-settings` by removing the redundant `General API Settings` and `Server Settings` cards.\n   - Kept language selection, PDF parsing profile, Unstructured API key, a clean link card to `screen-servers`, and hidden